.TH SDL_NODISCARD 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_NODISCARD \- A macro to tag a function\(aqs return value as critical.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_begin_code.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_NODISCARD [[nodiscard]]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a hint to the compiler that a function\(aqs return value should not be ignored\[char46]
.PP
If an NODISCARD function\(aqs return value is thrown away (the function is called as if it returns
.BR void ),
the compiler will issue a warning\[char46]
.PP
While it\(aqs generally good practice to check return values for errors, often times legitimate programs do not for good reasons\[char46] Be careful about what functions are tagged as NODISCARD\[char46] It operates best when used on a function that\(aqs failure is surprising and catastrophic; a good example would be a program that checks the return values of all its file write function calls but not the call to close the file, which it assumes incorrectly never fails\[char46]
.PP
Function callers that want to throw away a NODISCARD return value can call the function with a
.BR (void)
cast, which informs the compiler the act is intentional\[char46]
.PP
On compilers without nodiscard support, this is defined to nothing\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

